course: dictionary
lesson: 11023
title: Waving: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Waving is a word you already know, but it can mean several things. The words around it tell you which meaning fits. A word with many meanings is a good reason to check the context.
explain: «The waving flag in the Moon landing video wobbled because astronauts twisted its pole.» Here waving means moving from side to side or up and down in the air. The flag was moving, not a person saying hello.
explain: «Real drowning is often silent, with the head low and no waving, so if someone looks wrong, shout for the lifeguard at once.» Here waving means moving your arms to get attention. A person in trouble in the water may not wave, so you must watch for signs that someone is in danger.
fact: Waving means moving something from side to side or up and down, like waving a flag.
fact: Waving your hand can say hello or goodbye.
fact: Waving an arm can get a lifeguard's attention when someone is in trouble in the sea.
fact: «Waving» can also mean moving gently with the wind, like grass or a flag.
fact: Waving something away means refusing it or ignoring it.
exercise: «The waving flag in the Moon landing video wobbled.» What does waving mean here? | *Moving from side to side or up and down in the air | Refusing something | Saying hello to the astronauts | Shouting for help
exercise: Lucy stands on the pier, waving at her gran on the boat. What is she doing? | Swimming fast | *Saying hello or goodbye | Pulling in a fish | Pushing the boat away
exercise: «Real drowning is often silent, with no waving.» What does this tell you? | *A person in trouble may not wave, so you must watch for signs | Waving never happens in water | Drowning people always wave loudly | Waving means you are happy
test: Mum says, «Wave goodbye to Grandad!» What does waving mean? | Playing a game | *Moving your hand to say goodbye | Moving a flag in the wind | Ignoring a question
test: In «The grass was waving in the breeze», waving means: | Shouting for help | *Moving gently with the wind, like grass | Refusing a gift | Shaking a hand at someone
exam: Priya sees an arm waving above the waves far out at sea. What does this most likely mean? | The swimmer is saying hello to a friend | The swimmer is waving someone away | The swimmer is practising a dance | *The swimmer may need help and wants the lifeguard's attention
